From: Shazad Hussain <quic_shazhuss@quicinc.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Dec 2024 20:32:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PENDING: scsi: ufs: qcom: Enable sa8255p platform

Qualcomm platform sa8255p has remote firmware to configure platform
resource configurations like clocks, voltages and PHY.

Modeled power domain is used to abstract resources in firmware and
SCMI power protocol is used to request resource operations.

Runtime PM framework APIs such as pm_runtime_get/put_sync are used
to invoke appropriate power_on and power_off calls from kernel.

Prepare support for the sa8255p variant by adding the required
ufs_hba_qcom_fmr_vops to a new ufs_hba_variant_ops struct then
passing it through the compatible match data.

Change-Id: I275faa94b60bff71d87a8768d61d180e32d201fe
Co-developed-by: Nikunj Kela <quic_nkela@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Nikunj Kela <quic_nkela@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Shazad Hussain <quic_shazhuss@quicinc.com>
---
